     The pptthhrreeaadd__mmaaiinn__nnpp() function is used in userland threads environment to
     identify the initial thread.  Its semantics is similar to the Solaris's
     tthhrr__mmaaiinn() function.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The pptthhrreeaadd__mmaaiinn__nnpp() function returns 1 if the calling thread is the
     initial thread, 0 if the calling thread is not the initial thread, and -1
     if the thread's initialization has not yet completed.

